      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos\\left(x-2\\pi\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ or $\\cos x$.\n\nUse the formula\n\n$$\n\\cos(u-v)=\\cos u\\cos v+\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nand the exact values $\\cos(2\\pi)=1$ and $\\sin(2\\pi)=0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u-v)=\\cos u\\cos v+\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nWith $u=x$ and $v=2\\pi$, the exact values are $\\cos(2\\pi)=1$ and $\\sin(2\\pi)=0$. Substitute and collect the terms in the requested order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos\\left(x-2\\pi\\right)&=\\cos x\\cos\\left(2\\pi\\right)+\\sin x\\sin\\left(2\\pi\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\cdot\\left(1\\right)+\\sin x\\cdot\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
