    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2f1d5717-9e8e-58d2-bf00-f64b58dd717d",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos\\left(t+\\pi\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin t$ or $\\cos t$.\n\nUse the formula\n\n$$\n\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nand the exact values $\\cos(\\pi)=-1$ and $\\sin(\\pi)=0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the sum formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u+v)=\\cos u\\cos v-\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nWith $u=t$ and $v=\\pi$, the exact values are $\\cos(\\pi)=-1$ and $\\sin(\\pi)=0$. Substitute and collect the terms in the requested order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos\\left(t+\\pi\\right)&=\\cos t\\cos\\left(\\pi\\right)-\\sin t\\sin\\left(\\pi\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos t\\cdot\\left(-1\\right)-\\sin t\\cdot\\left(0\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\cos t.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
